
## Setup for a new user

Please use  `sbatch_interpole_multiproc.sh`, it is faster, I keep the other for history. 

You should copy the entire folder to your own home directory. Then run
`sbatch sbatch_interpole_multiproc.sh` 


Please check the file edit `config/ALPX3.yaml` (or copy it to a new domain file):
* `paths.input_folder` / `paths.output_folder` — where to read the raw
  files from and write the interpolated output to for this run.
* `site.gl_bin_dir` — path to the `gl` binary. Please use mine for now.
* `input_files.*` — the naming convention of the source files
  (prefix/suffix filter and the regex/format used to read their embedded
  timestamp). Adjust if your input files aren't named like the ones here.
  `era5_2*` The prefix from the era5 files
* `domain.*` and `vertical_levels.*` — the target geometry and its
  vertical levels; do not change if you use the arome-CNRM config with 60 levels. 

`CONFIG` in the sbatch script picks which of these files to use; the
scripts also accept `--input_folder`/`--output_folder` on the command
line if you want to override the config for a one-off run without
editing it.

## Important sites:

* parameter database: https://codes.ecmwf.int/grib/param-db/
* MARS user documentation: https://confluence.ecmwf.int/display/UDOC/MARS+user+documentation
* ECMWF web api
* Archive catalogue: https://confluence.ecmwf.int/display/WEBAPI/ECMWF+Web+API+Home
* ERA5 catalog: https://apps.ecmwf.int/data-catalogues/era5/?class=ea
* tuto: https://confluence.ecmwf.int/display/UDOC/HRES%3A+Atmospheric+%28oper%29%2C+Model+level+%28ml%29%2C+Forecast+%28fc%29%3A+Guidelines+to+write+efficient+MARS+requests

## Parameters needed for arome: 
* Atmosphere
    * param=130/138/155, # t, d, vo
    * param=133, # specific humidity
    * param=152, # LNSP
    * WIND U/v: 131, 132
* Surface: 
    * param=27/28/29/30/32/33/39/40/41/42/129/139/141/160/161/162/170/172/183/236,
